{"created": "2025-07-21T12:56:55.622566+00:00", "modified": "2026-02-16T16:26:49.702206+00:00", "id": 15053268, "conceptrecid": "15053267", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.15053268", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.15053267", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15053268", "metadata": {"title": "VelRecover: An Interactive Python Tool for Building Velocity Models from Sparse Velocity Picks in Legacy Seismic Sections", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.15053268", "publication_date": "2025-07-30", "description": "<p><strong>VelRecover</strong> is a GUI based tool designed to interpolate 2D seismic velocity data from sparse velocity picks found in vintage seismic reflection sections. Results can be exported as text or binary files, suitable for further seismic processing workflows. The tool requires a SEGY file and a text file containing velocities, CDPs, and TWTs as input.</p>\n<p>Check the GitHub repository for detailed information and the latest development release:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://github.com/a-pertuz/velrecover\">https://github.com/a-pertuz/velrecover</a></p>\n<h3>Installation &amp; Running</h3>\n<p>To install <strong>VelRecover</strong>, you can:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Using pip</strong>:</p>\n<div>\n<div><code>pip install velrecover\n</code></div>\n</div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>From Source</strong>:</p>\n<div>\n<div><code>pip install git+https://github.com/username/velrecover.git</code></div>\n</div>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Once installed, run the application by typing:</p>\n<div>\n<div><code>velrecover</code></div>\n</div>\n<p>Alternatively, you can download the zip and run&nbsp;the file <code>run_src_velrecover.py</code>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Pertuz, Alejandro", "affiliation": "Universidad Complutense de Madrid", "orcid": "0000-0003-2498-1854"}, {"name": "Benito, M. Isabel", "affiliation": "Universidad Complutense de Madrid", "orcid": "0000-0002-8711-0864"}, {"name": "LLANES ESTRADA, PILAR", "affiliation": null, "orcid": "0000-0001-6334-3711"}, {"name": "Suarez-Gonzalez, Pablo", "affiliation": null, "orcid": "0000-0002-2370-5017"}, {"name": "Garc\u00eda-Mart\u00edn, Mart\u00edn", "affiliation": "Universidad Rey Juan Carlos", "orcid": "0009-0004-2599-167X"}], "custom": {"code:codeRepository": "https://github.com/a-pertuz/velrecover", "code:programmingLanguage": [{"id": "python", "title": {"en": "Python"}}], "code:developmentStatus": {"id": "active", "title": {"en": "Active"}}}, "resource_type": {"title": "Software", "type": "software"}, "license": {"id": "gpl-3.0-or-later"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "15053267"}}]}}, "title": "VelRecover: An Interactive Python Tool for Building Velocity Models from Sparse Velocity Picks in Legacy Seismic Sections", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/15053268", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/15053268", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/15053268?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15053268", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15053268", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.15053268", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/15053268/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/15053267", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/15053267", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15053267", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.15053267", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:15053268/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:15053268/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/15053268/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/15053268/media-files", "archive": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/15053268/files-archive", "archive_media": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/15053268/media-files-archive", "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/15053268/vers